WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.700
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.200
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.400
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:02.680
<i>I'm travelling with Jasmine and Barda to take back the gems that were stolen by the Shadow Lord.</i>

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.620
<i>And there are only two gems left!</i>

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.730
<i>However, the Shadow Lord is now hunting for a boy, a man and a wild girl with a black bird.</i>

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.310
<i>Why am I the 'wild one', anyway?
Honestly, the Shadow Lord has no taste.</i>

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.210
<i>Our journey is sure to become
more perilous from now on!</i>

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:24.610
<i>Right now, we're headed to the Maze of the Beast, where the sixth gem is hidden!</i>

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.300
Barda...!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:23.670
I know.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:31.820
Good evening, everyone.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:38.610
We're very sorry to disturb
you from your peaceful sleep.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.600
But we need you to pay a special
toll, if you wouldn't mind.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.750
It's the bandits!

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.010
C-Calm down, Sandra...!

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.780
My subordinates will come
to collect it from you now.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.780
So do be sensible and
cooperate with us, alright?

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:58.050
You can pay us in gems, in money,
or with anything that can be sold!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.800
I don't mind if you want to pay
with your lives instead, either.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.590
Seems like the captain won't
be coming out to help us.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.640
He's probably quite used
to situations like these.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.370
So this is the true meaning behind
'every man for himself', then!

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.720
This lot are quite a handful...

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.100
What should we do, Barda?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.700
Let's just do as they say for the time being.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.400
But then...!

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.230
We can't risk bringing harm to the passengers
by starting a fight here, can we?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.730
We'll get our chance. Just wait for my signal.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:29.400
Got it.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.470
Hey you! What are you whispering about?!
Hurry up and hand over your valuables!

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:37.920
Oh, I'm sorry good sir, but
we are just poor fellows...

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.000
So as far as 'valuables' are concerned...

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.740
...this is all we have...

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.240
Tch...! Can't be helped then...

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.590
But now that I get a good look at you
three, you do seem pretty poor...

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.600
Not too bad, Monkey!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.530
Are you taking me for a fool?

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.430
Now, you'll hand that
over as well, won't you?

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.790
This seems valuable enough.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.000
Not too bad, Monkey.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.300
What now?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.000
It's fine. We can just get them back later.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:19.600
This is a nice gemstone you have here.
This should be worth a fair sum.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.600
Anything but that! This necklace is
almost as precious as my life!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.200
So you want me to take it from
your corpse instead, then?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.710
S-Sandra...!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.900
What the heck is this?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:40.500
T...That's my working tool. If you take that
away, then how am I supposed to...

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.300
So I just have to turn this lever, huh?

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.200
This is pretty neat!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.520
Y-Yeah, isn't it?

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.740
I'll be taking it, then.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.900
You can't!

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.160
Please have mercy, good sir!
I won't be able to work if you-

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:55.900
Like I care!

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.600
Hold it!

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.100
Guys!

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.430
Take a look at what I found!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.100
Nooo!

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.140
Only the prettiest lady can
wear the prettiest dress...

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.380
Please stop...!

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.310
In other words, someone like me!

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:16.800
What was that?!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.730
If you want it so much, then help yourself!

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:26.010
As I thought, wearing something I'm not used to doesn't feel too great.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:29.000
I see. A wild cat in sheep's clothing, huh?

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.500
You've sure got guts...!

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.300
Now!

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.470
Do your worst!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:47.790
Damn you...!

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.120
Stop darting around!

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.980
Hey, what the hell are you doing, Monkey?!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.280
Very good!

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.480
You bastard monkey!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.800
Now then, how about we
give this another try?

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.200
You... where have I seen that face before...?

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.360
That's right! Aren't you the brat
who's always at Doom's side?!

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.100
And what about it?!

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:24.810
Shit...

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.810
These guys are strong...!

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.640
Okay okay, that's enough.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.040
Don't you care about what
happens to this woman?

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.800
Come on. Hurry up and drop your weapons!

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:46.400
I'm not a patient woman, you know?
Or do you want to try me? I'll do it!

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.520
Drop those swords. Now!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.000
What's so funny?!

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.260
It's an Ol!

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.300
Run!

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:24.940
Dain!

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:40.700
Barda...

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:43.600
Polipan...?

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.100
Oh no! He got the Belt!!

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.380
Jasmi-

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.230
I'm sure that the Grey Guards
will pay a hefty sum for you.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.320
You damned monster!

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:07.390
Barda!

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.500
That lot should be done for by now.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:43.830
Let me take this for you. This belt is
way too good for some monkey.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.050
Woah there.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:54.910
Am I...

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.240
...really going to die here...?

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:10.980
Did that do the trick...?

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.790
The one thing I absolutely can't stand are Ols!

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:35.060
Jasmine?

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:36.470
Jasmine!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.480
Jasmine!!

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.270
Jasmine... Please open your mouth, Jasmine!

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.810
Drinking this will definitely
make you well again!

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.500
Thank goodness...

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.040
Seems like she'll pull through, huh?

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:05.980
Where's Barda?!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.100
Barda...

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:17.630
He's either drowned or been eaten
by the river snakes, I suppose.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.790
That can't be!

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:20.500
Just give it up.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.500
It couldn't be...

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.290
Please don't think bad of us, alright?

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:48.740
As long as you two are being targeted by Ols,
we really have no choice but to do this.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:49.900
I understand that...

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.950
But really, what luck.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:56.300
Not only were we raided by bandits,
but even our polipan went missing.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.810
This is just too much...

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.100
Now that you mention it,
where do you think it went?

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:03.520
How should I know? It left
with the bandits, after all.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:07.100
And as a result, here I am
having to row this boat.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:09.200
Really, that ungrateful old guy.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:10.900
Heave-ho!

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.240
Well then, have a safe trip!

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:16.280
Sorry, but blame the Ols for your misfortune.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.000
What are we going to do now...?

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:57.100
We have to save Dain soon, right...?

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:03.200
I know, the Belt! We can borrow the
Belt's power at times like these!

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.200
We can't.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.700
Why not...?

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:10.460
That Polipan stole the Belt when
we were busy with the Ol...

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:11.440
What?!

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.070
And that Polipan has gone off somewhere
together with the bandits.

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.600
Then what are we supposed to do now?!

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:24.310
Well, I tried to imagine what Barda
would say in a situation like this...

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:30.270
"We must rest and recover for now."

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.000
And whatever Barda said would always end up
being right in the end, wouldn't you say?

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:40.030
Always...

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:42.780
Lief...

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:50.490
Hey, what's the matter?

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:52.800
You two look like you've
seen a ghost or something.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:54.970
Barda...!

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:54.970
-Barda...!

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.430
The Belt was stolen...?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.680
Yeah, that polipan took it from me...

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.000
Can't we just buy a new one?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:05.560
Huh?

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:08.300
That's not what I meant.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:12.820
That monkey took my belt, including the
Belt of Deltora that was hidden inside it!

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.830
The Belt of Deltora...

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:19.100
We need to locate the bandits' hideout
and take the Belt back from them!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.600
I think I know where that is.

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.400
Here.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.890
What's that?!

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.400
One of them dropped it back on the ferry.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.900
Wait, this mark...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.700
Could that be the location
of the Maze of the Beast?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.800
Then this is...!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.300
That's right.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.700
This is where we're headed...

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:42.670
But, why did the bandits
have this map on them?

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.780
Could it be that they're after the gem as well?

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.470
T-That's right! It is valuable, after all!

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:51.330
Then we need to hurry! It would be
bad if they got it before us!

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.620
Hold on, now. I understand
why you want to hurry.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.940
But what's most important
for us right now is...

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.570
"...to rest and recover," right?

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:01.280
Exactly.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:05.100
"What Barda says is always
correct in the end," right?

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.240
Yeah!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.690
Boy am I starving!

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.420
It should be ready now, right?
Let's hurry up and eat!

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:42.580
It's way too soon. Can't you
see that they're still raw?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.190
Yep, this is fine. Why don't
you guys eat too?

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:51.410
It's good, you know?

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.530
I wonder if Dain is okay...

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.070
He's probably fine.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:36.330
One of the bandits said something about
selling him to the Grey Guards, after all.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.440
And in what way is that 'fine'?!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:42.570
Because Dain is an important hostage to them!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:43.970
How could you say that?!

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:48.930
Don't you realise that Dain could be in the
hands of the Grey Guards at this very moment?!

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.990
And what can we do about that
if we're all the way over here?!

00:16:55.880 --> 00:17:00.940
All we can do right now is just keep hoping that
Dain is safe at the bandit's hideout, right?!

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.100
I'm sorry...

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.820
You're right...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.740
We can only pile on what we
can do now, little by little...

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.490
That's right!

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.000
Piling is best!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.420
First pile, second pile, third pile,

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.800
fourth pile, fifth pile, sixth pile.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.000
The more we pile, the higher it's going to be.

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:25.490
And in the end, we will be able to save Dain.

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:29.200
Furthermore, if everything goes well,
it will be less DAINgerous for him!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.850
Was that... a pun?

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.200
What do you think? Pretty funny, right?

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.520
The Belt...

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.430
What if we can't find those bandits...?

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:00.150
Or what if they sold the gems
before we could reach them...?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.860
No, you can't let yourself focus
on negative thoughts like these!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.450
We will definitely take
the Belt back. We must!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:16.780
Barda?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.740
Lief?

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:21.320
Shouldn't you be asleep by now?

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.940
You need to rest so you can
be ready in the morning.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.660
Yeah, I know.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:29.220
Good night.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:50.690
Barda!

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:53.700
Barda!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.000
What's the matter? Are you feeling unwell?

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.100
No, it's nothing really.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.400
I just got a little lost in thought, that's all.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.680
Don't you think Barda's
been acting weird lately?

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:10.190
He may just be tired;
he went through a lot after all.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:11.870
I hope you're right...

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.700
Sorry, sorry.

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:15.400
Are you really alright, Barda?

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:16.800
Fit as a fiddle.

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.500
Hey, Barda.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.960
It's been three days since we started walking,
but we still haven't reached the sea...?

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.500
It's just up ahead.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.170
How do you know that?

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:27.970
You didn't notice it, Jasmine?

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.080
Notice what?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.760
The smell of salt has been
in the air for a while now.

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:32.730
Salt?

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.350
So this is the scent of the sea, then?

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.600
Oh, right.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:42.020
I forgot that you've never
been to the sea before.

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:45.180
Also, these types of trees
only grow close to the sea.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.220
Really?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.890
So we'll be able to see the ocean
once we pass these trees, then?

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:51.900
I'll be going ahead then!

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:53.700
Geez...

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.400
Wait for us, Jasmine!

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:13.470
We've finally made it here...

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:16.390
Hey now, don't you start
forgetting our mission.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:17.550
Of course not.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.800
It should be around here...

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.560
Over there, do you think?

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:32.990
Yeah, that must be it! Let's go!

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.900
There should be a guardian protecting
this gem too. Be careful.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.120
There doesn't seem to be anyone here...

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.390
Don't let down your guard.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:02.600
Wait.

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:04.060
Look down here.

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:06.520
Footprints?

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:09.300
Seems they've been here before us.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:11.770
I just saw something glimmer!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:20.270
This is a jewellery box, right?

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:25.750
Yeah. The sixth gem that we're looking for
was probably stored inside this box.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.590
Then could it be that
the bandits took it first?

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:31.240
That's impossible!

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:34.700
The gem is supposed to be
protected by a guardian!

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:35.800
Then...

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.800
...this means that the bandits
have defeated the guardian.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:42.810
We need to catch up to them right away!

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:45.940
Right, they can't be that far ahead!

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:46.850
It's no use.

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:51.700
I only brought you this far because I
thought that you'd be of some use,

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.150
but this should be far enough.

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:53.980
Barda?

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.400
Our journey together ends here.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:00.990
What are you talking about, Barda?!

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:04.970
Our cause was already lost from
the moment you lost the Belt.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:07.810
So we had best accept our defeat right here.

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:08.750
Barda...

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:12.650
I will not! Even if I have to go by myself!

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:15.000
I will definitely recover the Belt!

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.000
There is nothing you can do at this point.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.200
I still won't give in until the very end!

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:24.500
Then, I have no choice
but to stop you by force!

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:50.360
Typesetting

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.300
<i>The Ralads.</i>

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:11.300
<i>One of the Seven Tribes of Deltora.</i>

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:14.350
<i>They are talented carpenters
who also built the Palace of Del.</i>

00:24:14.350 --> 00:24:16.990
<i>The Sorceress Thaegan robbed
them of their voices,</i>

00:24:16.990 --> 00:24:19.750
<i>but they have since recovered them,
thanks to Lief and the others.</i>

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:23.800
We met with an outrageous situation
after we reunited with Barda!

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:27.220
And in the end, Jasmine and I
were captured by the bandits...

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:31.390
Then, we were finally able to meet up with Dain again at their hideout, but...

00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:34.740
The Bandits' Feast

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:34.740
Next time, 'The Bandits' Feast'.

